Frequently Asked Coding Questions — Java Streams

1. Find the second-highest salary from a list of employees

int secondHighestSalary = employees.stream()
        .map(Employee::getSalary)
        .distinct()
        .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())
        .skip(1)
        .findFirst()
        .orElseThrow();

Explanation

1. "map()" → extracts salaries.
2. "distinct()" → removes duplicate salaries.
3. "sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())" → sorts highest to lowest.
4. "skip(1)" → skips the highest salary.
5. "findFirst()" → gets the second-highest salary.

---

2. Find the highest salary in each department

Map<String, Employee> result = employees.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
                Employee::getDepartment,
                Collectors.collectingAndThen(
                        Collectors.maxBy(Comparator.comparing(Employee::getSalary)),
                        Optional::get
                )
        ));

If only the salary is required

Map<String, Integer> result = employees.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
                Employee::getDepartment,
                Collectors.collectingAndThen(
                        Collectors.maxBy(Comparator.comparing(Employee::getSalary)),
                        e -> e.get().getSalary()
                )
        ));

