20. Find common elements between two lists

List<Integer> common = list1.stream()
        .filter(list2::contains)
        .distinct()
        .toList();

Example

List 1:
[1, 2, 3, 4]

List 2:
[3, 4, 5, 6]

Common:
[3, 4]

Better approach for large lists

Convert the second list into a "Set":

Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>(list2);

List<Integer> common = list1.stream()
        .filter(set::contains)
        .distinct()
        .toList();

This avoids repeatedly scanning "list2".

