"map()"| Transform elements
"mapToInt()"| Convert to "IntStream"
"sorted()"| Sort elements
"distinct()"| Remove duplicates
"limit()"| Take first N elements
"skip()"| Skip first N elements
"findFirst()"| Get first element
"max()"| Find maximum
"min()"| Find minimum
"sum()"| Calculate sum
"average()"| Calculate average
"groupingBy()"| Group elements
"partitioningBy()"| Partition into two groups
"toMap()"| Convert stream into Map
"counting()"| Count elements
"collect()"| Collect stream results

Interview Pattern Recognition

Most of these questions can be solved by recognizing a small number of patterns:

1. Highest / Lowest
   
   - "max()"
   - "min()"
   - "sorted()"

2. Nth Highest
   
   - "distinct()"
   - "sorted(reverseOrder())"
   - "skip()"
   - "findFirst()"

3. Frequency
   
   - "groupingBy()"
   - "counting()"

4. Grouping
   
   - "groupingBy()"

5. Even / Odd
   
   - "partitioningBy()"

6. Filtering
   
   - "filter()"

7. Transformation
   
   - "map()"

8. Duplicate Removal
   
   - "distinct()"

9. List → Map
   
   - "Collectors.toMap()"

10. Top N

- "sorted()"
- "limit()"

